  "term": "cutoff score",
  "definition": "A cutoff score is the chosen point on a screening measure that is used to separate people into groups, such as likely having or not having a condition. The best cutoff can vary with the purpose of the test because different score thresholds change the balance between false positives, sensitivity, and specificity.",
